{#
After a drop on a label, or a tick or untick in the toolbar's label menu.

`leaves: false`, and that one flag is the whole difference from
thread/status/_move.stream.html.twig. A label is additive — the conversation
gains it and stays exactly where it was — so the rows are REDRAWN rather than
removed, which is also what puts the new chip beside the subject without a
reload.

The toast still names the destination, for the same reason a move's does: the
drop was aimed by pointer at a sidebar row a couple of dozen pixels tall. It is
the more necessary of the two here, if anything — a move at least announces
itself by the row disappearing, and this one changes a chip most of the way
across the screen from where the pointer let go.

Variables:
  count      how many conversations were labelled
  threads    the conversations, so their rows can be redrawn with the new chip
  label      what was attached, for the toast
  attach     optional, default true; false when the menu took the label off
  undoToken  optional; puts an Undo in the toast
#}
{% set attach  = attach ?? true %}
{% set message = (attach ? 'toast.labelled' : 'toast.unlabelled')|trans({ '%label%': label|label_name }) %}

{% include 'thread/status/_bulk.stream.html.twig' with {
    count:   count,
    threads: threads,
    leaves:  false,
} only %}

{% if undoToken|default(null) is not null %}
    {% include 'thread/status/_undo_toast.stream.html.twig' with { message: message, undoToken: undoToken } only %}
{% else %}
    {% include '_partials/_toast.stream.html.twig' with { message: message } only %}
{% endif %}
